  "review_summary": "**Triage Summary:**\n\nThe findings split into two actionable categories: (1) **Fixable vulnerabilities** \u2014 CVE-2024-2398 (libcurl HIGH) and CVE-2022-37434 (zlib CRITICAL) both have available patches and should be prioritized for immediate dependency updates; (2) **Unfixable or low-risk findings** \u2014 the majority are either unfixed CVEs from 2026 (likely false positives or future-dated entries requiring validation) or have negligible EPSS scores (<0.03), including CVE-2019-8457 (libdb5.3, no fix available but rarely exploited in practice). The perl-base and libc findings all show EPSS <0.005 with no fixes, indicating minimal practical risk.\n\n**Recommended Action:** Approve this build with conditions \u2014 immediately schedule updates for libcurl and zlib in the next release cycle, validate the 2026-dated CVEs against your scanner's data source (likely data quality issues), and defer the unfixed legacy CVEs (libdb5.3, libc, libssh2, perl) unless your threat model specifically requires them.",
